 Today's newsletter is 775 words, a 3-minute read. 

 📉 The dashboard: The S&amp;P 500 closed down 1.1%.

 Chipmakers fell for an eighth straight session, the longest slide since 2008, Bloomberg notes . Zoom out: The S&amp;P closed down 1.9% for the week. It's now up 11.9% on the year. 🥶 Today's stock spotlight: CoreWeave (-11.9%) tumbled again, extending the neocloud provider's losses to 25% this week amid growing concerns about the debt financing AI's massive infrastructure buildout.

 
 
