 4. 🏀 Don&#x27;t bet on it 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 NBA commissioner Adam Silver. Photo: Chase Stevens/Las Vegas Review-Journal/Tribune News Service via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sportsbooks that partner with the NBA will stop accepting certain bets deemed too susceptible to manipulation after the league asked them to do so.

 🚫 State of play: Newly banned bets include:

 Parlays involving multiple bets on a single NBA player to perform below expectations in different statistical categories, known as "unders." Unders on players expected to play fewer than 12 minutes in the game. "The NBA also directed its authorized gambling operators, including DraftKings and FanDuel, not to offer bets on the winner of the opening tip" and "players to miss specific shots," ESPN reported . 🤨 The big picture: The move comes after multiple incidents raised suspicions of players intentionally underperforming to help win bets.

 Yes, but: The NBA doesn't have any official partnerships with prediction markets, which aren't required to follow the league's requests.

 
 
